## 2026-09-30T09:56:00+05:30 corrects C1 — the plan's tokenizer ORDER is wrong
Plan Phase 2 step 2 says "normalise, then match added tokens against the *normalised*
text". Measured against HF tokenizers 0.22.2, that is WRONG for this checkpoint:
  tk.encode('  x')            -> ['▁','▁x']       (two single ▁, NOT the ▁▁ added token id 139)
  tk.encode('▁▁x')            -> ['▁▁','▁x']     (raw ▁ DOES match)
  tk.encode('    four spaces')-> ['▁','▁','▁','▁four','▁spaces']
The reason: all 249 added tokens in this tokenizer.json carry `normalized: false`, which in
HF means "match against the ORIGINAL input". And the vocab has NO raw-space added tokens --
the space-run tokens are written as U+2581 runs (ids 139..168) -- so a space run can never
match once the Replace normaliser has rewritten it. The existing C++ pipeline already does
added-token matching FIRST on the raw text (tokenizer_bbpe.cpp:563-612), so the correct
change is SMALLER than the plan assumed: add norm==2 (Replace) and a Metaspace pre-tokenizer,
keep the added-token stage where it is.
MetaSpace behaviour measured (probe with added_tokens removed):
  split keeps the ▁ with the FOLLOWING piece and drops empty pieces:
    '▁▁x' -> ['▁','▁x'] ; '▁▁▁x' -> ['▁','▁','▁x'] ; 'x▁y' -> ['▁x','▁y']
  prepend ▁ to the whole segment iff it does not already start with ▁.
  88 added tokens are strict prefixes of other added tokens -> leftmost-longest is load-bearing.
  Only `<mask>` has lstrip:true. No single_word, no rstrip, none have raw spaces in content.

