## 2026-09-30T11:12:00+05:30 decision D1 — tokenizer pipeline order (corrects plan Phase 2)
Plan said: "normalise, then match added tokens against the NORMALISED text".
MEASURED AGAINST HF: added tokens here all carry `normalized: false`, which in
HF means "match the ORIGINAL input". The vocab has no raw-space added tokens at
all -- the space runs are U+2581 runs (ids 139..168) -- so a space run can never
match after the Replace normaliser rewrote it. Evidence:
    tk('  x')             -> ['▁','▁x']        (not the ▁▁ added token, id 139)
    tk('▁▁x')             -> ['▁▁','▁x']      (raw ▁ DOES match)
So the EXISTING C++ order (added-token split on raw text, first) is already right.
The change is smaller than the plan assumed: add norm==2 (Replace) and a Metaspace
pre-tokenizer. No reordering of the added-token stage.

