## 2026-09-30T14:06:00+05:30 corrects C3 — the plan's "throw if [blob/config] disagree" on
### the special ids is WRONG, and following it would make the model unloadable
Plan: "Read all five from the encoder config, never from the blob, and throw if
they disagree." Measured: they DO disagree, by design of the derivation.
  blob derives cls_id = first of {[CLS], <s>, <|endoftext|>}; laya's vocab has
  <s> at 204 -> cls_id 204. Config says cls_token_id = 1. Same for sep (</s> at
  213 vs 1). So a throw makes laya unloadable over a NAME GUESS being a name
  guess.
Resolution: the container wins, the blob's values are overwritten, the
disagreement is PRINTED, and the refusal that IS correct is "the container's id
is not in the vocabulary at all".
Also: `AnyTokenizer::encode()` now REFUSES on an arch=4 container by name. Every
other backend here is an embedding encoder where the facade's wrap-and-pad policy
is right; arch=4's prompt is assembled token by token with its specials in hand,
so the facade is not merely different, it is wrong.

