## 2026-09-30T14:45:00+05:30 note E4 — the Linux NPU toolchain, three discoveries
1. aiecc shells out to `xclbinutil`; it lives in /opt/xilinx/xrt/bin and is NOT
   on PATH. Fails 35 steps into the first shape otherwise.
2. PyXRT must be importable. mlir-aie picks its tensor class at IMPORT: XRT's
   if `pyxrt` imports, CPU-only otherwise. CPU-only REJECTS device="npu", and
   device="cpu" is NOT a fix -- it makes pretiled_array() try to RUN the design
   ("Cannot run kernel; DefaultNPURuntime not set"). A pyxrt built for
   cpython-314 exists at
   ~/repos/xdna-driver/xrt/build/Release/opt/xilinx/xrt/python/
   utilities/build-design-sets.py finds it by CPython tag and sets PYTHONPATH.
3. `nohup ... &` from the bash tool gets killed when the call times out. Use
   `setsid nohup ... & disown` for the multi-minute build.
